From 412da384f1769bbb1bb0b73a41d4550d17d93396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:16:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Amlogic S905X5 BL201 reference board

Add the Amlogic BL201 reference board, with the S905X5 (S6) SoC, using
the S6 packaging.

The binaries come from the Amlogic S6 bootloader release:
- bb1st, blob-bl2e, blob-bl2x: bl2/bin/s6/s905x5
- blob-bl31: bl31/bl31_2.7/bin/s6/s905x5
- blob-bl32: bl32/bl32_3.18/bin/s6/s905x5
- blob-bl40: bl40/bin/s6/s905x5
- device-fip-header.bin: soc/templates/s6/s905x5
- acpu-imagetool: fip/s6/binary-tool, zstd: fip/tools
all in the default rsa-mldsa.rsa-mldsa signing scheme of fip/s6.

bl30.bin is built from bl30/rtos_sdk for the bl201_s905x5 board and the
aocpu product (riscv-none-embed-gcc 8.2.0-2.2, as set in
soc/riscv/s6/toolchain_path.cmake), with the call to vIRInit() in
boards/riscv/bl201_s905x5/power.c updated to the drivers_aocpu/ir API
of the release, which no longer takes the IR mode (NEC is the only
mode).

acs.bin is built from the vendor U-Boot s6/firmware/acs sources and
board/amlogic/s6_bl201/firmware/{timing,ddr_timing}.c, with the
s6_bl201 board configuration, as the vendor acs Makefile does.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
